        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE REHNQUIST: We'll hear argument next in Number 02-271, the Dow Chemical Company v. Daniel Raymond Stephenson."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We rely on four propositions in this case. First, there is a long final judgment in the Agent Orange litigation that binds a class which by its terms includes respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "respondents? It's sort of hard to find, looking back at the settlement agreement and the orders that were entered, that the people in respondent's category were thought to be covered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Well, Justice O'Connor, notice in this case -- I think as the case comes to this Court, the Court certainly cannot decide this case on the principle that the notice was constitutionally inadequate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Waxman, I'd like to stop you right there, exposure itself has been said to be injurious."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Why? Why?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Now, to know whether they're right or wrong about that, I guess I have to read 500,000 pages of this settlement hearing and find out everything about this case in order to decide whether they're right or wrong --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm just pointing out that Amchem didn't redetermine adequacy as a factual matter. It concluded that as a matter of law --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smoger",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, Mr. Stephenson had none of those, and let me tell you why. To begin with, we're talking about the question of representation and the adequacy of representation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Judge Weinstein certified the class, there was still no representatives, and they were said that - - he asked the plaintiffs' lawyers to find them. It was certified without any single representatives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smoger",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. SMOGER: No, because Ivy did -- was eligible for money from the settlement funds. The settlement funds ran out in 1994. That's why it's different. So they had a very specific holding on efficiency in -- in -- before."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Smoger",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In -- that -- Judge Weinstein had said that that reserve fund would be stay -- would be held for futures after 1994. In 1994, that reserve fund at petitioner Dow's request was then given to the -- to the class assistance program, so the reserve fund that was supposed to be there to 2008, and had the capability of paying some money for post 1994 claimants, was also depleted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: It's very odd that abuse of discretion is the standard on direct review, and on collateral review you have a more generous standard. That's very odd."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, but in some cases the fact that he wasn't there has not -- is not going to mean that he can get de novo review, I would think, of the determination that he's bound by the class settlement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: Justice O'Connor, the -- the Isaacson case can't just be remanded, because we assert jurisdiction under 1442."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Waxman",
      "case_id": "2002-02-271",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e4938a23cecb644fb8785cdf62701d7722d07a29230fe9a633981fb32b5091a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e4938a23cecb-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "should, a) give tremendous deference, and because the issue has been decided, because the consequences of not giving deference would be unbelievably unsettling."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
